<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Telepar cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Telepar cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Salomon Brothers said on Thursday it was cutting its rating for Brazilian telephone company Telepar SA to hold from buy.</p>
<p>-- The downgrade was &quot;based on the stock's recent rally and its fair valuation relative to (Brazilian telephone company) Telemig TMG_p.SA,&quot; Salomon wrote in a March 19 report.</p>
<p>-- Telepar's preferred shares were unchanged at 708 reais in Sao Paulo. The ordinary shares were down 10.01 reais at 729.99.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
